ST CARRY: the mechanism moves prices in Jun-Sep and NOWHERE ELSE (2025 monthly delta 0,0,0,0,-0.006,-1.836,-2.448,-1.403,-1.276,-0.003,0,0 $/MWh), so MAY IS NOT REACHABLE BY IT — May-2025 goes +12.43 % -> +12.41 %, delta -0.006 $/MWh. May's CC availability deficit and the summer deficit are the SAME SYMPTOM WITH DIFFERENT CAUSES; 'one object, both signs' describes the symptom, not the cause, and the May half remains unexplained. CELLS: MISO K (built, solved, registered at miso-148 and PROMOTED to the keeper by owner decision). ERCOT '.' — structurally inapplicable, its CAMPD-bin fleet carries Nameplate_MW so there is no double count to repair. CAISO / PJM / NYISO / NEISO U — all four run plant_level_fleet with cc_nameplate_summer_derate armed, which routes CC through the per-plant measured ratio but leaves CT_PEAKER / CT_CHP on the flat derate over a net-summer base, i.e. the SAME double count is live and UNMEASURED on their CT classes. Rule 25 [R-ISO-SCOPE] / 28(d): no verdict transfers and no parameter crosses a boundary — the predicate is each plant's own published rating, never a fitted value; each lane measures its own exposure before arming.",
