nyiso-119 / caiso-186 / miso-148 discipline), so the default cache key is byte-stable and an armed run hashes distinctly. TESTED AT miso-159 (PREREG-miso159-commission-year-cod-fallback-2026-08-15.md, pushed and blob-verified BEFORE the construction was built): Phase-0 instrument gates on the production fleet path — V2 off-arm byte-inert (every classed row still 2010) PASS, V3 keeper fleet (n_gen 2929/2923/2923, 6 carry zones) PASS, S-CACHE distinct-key PASS, V1 armed-fleet per-class cap-weighted online_year vs the census truth PASS with the S-V1 excursion attributed (CT_CHP +1.015 yr on the LP-pmax basis is the BTM steam-following holdout's weighting, +0.011 yr on the census's own nameplate basis; unit tests tests/unit/data/test_campd_bins.py::TestCommissionYearCodFallback 4/4). P-1 census-derived reach bands MISSED LOW and are reported: the production-path truth is 2.13/2.46/2.87 GW annual and 1.31/1.48/1.64 GW summer (non-CHP, off−on) vs census arithmetic 3.55/3.95/4.37 and 2.06/2.27/2.49 — the census's uniform derate+share×wefor formula overstates coal's summer leg (drop_coal_pof zeroes coal summer WEFOR, so coal moves on DERATE alone) and prices nameplate where the LP prices net-summer pmax. CELLS: MISO — see the MISO shard for the tested verdict and A/B evidence (runs 2026-08-15-miso-159-control / 2026-08-15-miso-159-cod-vintage). ERCOT U — censused at exactly 0.000 GW effect for the fall-through-only replacement (its registry hits are untouched by construction), so arming is a measured no-op awaiting its own lane's decision; CAISO / PJM / NYISO / NEISO U — exposed on the same code path with censused magnitude, but rule 25 [R-ISO-SCOPE] / 28(d): no verdict transfers, each lane arms only after its own measurement.",
